Let $F$ be a set of sets of $\mathcal{X}$ and let $I$ be an $F$-capacity.
A set $s$ of $\mathcal{X}$ is said to be $I$-capacitable if for all $a < I(s)$, there exists a set $t \in F_\delta$ such that $t \subseteq s$ and $a \le I(t)$.
\end{definition}

